WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.260
We all love reading story books.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.000
Every story is framed with sentences, and

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.860
sentences are framed using words.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.130
And what are words made up of?

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.430
They are made up of letters!

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.160
If you notice, then everything around us is

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.640
made up of one or the other smaller entity.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.119
These small entities are called Basic units!

00:00:26.119 --> 00:00:29.732
Did you know, that even our body is made up

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:30.740
basic units?

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.980
Yes it is!

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.164
Although it appears to be one single body,

00:00:35.164 --> 00:00:37.400
it is actually made up of millions of basic

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:42.059
units coming together! what these units are called?

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.500
They are known as CELLS!

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.620
Cells come in different numbers to form our

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.320
body, rather, any living organism’s body.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.900
Can you guess the minimum number of cells

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.540
required to form an organism’s body?

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.800
Do you know the answer?

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.900
There are organisms which are made up of only

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:02.920
a single cell!

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.760
They are called the unicellular organisms!

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:11.220
Bacteria are one of the best examples of this category.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.340
what are organisms like us called then?

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.080
We belong to the category of multi-cellular organisms.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.360
Those having several cells to make up the

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.580
body are called multi-cellular organisms

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.240
Now the next important question is… if there

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.830
are so many cells in our body, then are all

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.040
of them exactly the same?

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.950
Of course NOT!

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:35.280
There are many number of cells in our body,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.520
and so are their types!

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.140
Look at these cells for example!

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.920
These look so different!

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:46.580
But astonishingly, all three are a part of our body!

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.544
This one is an ovum, this is a neuron and

00:01:49.544 --> 00:01:51.930
the last one is a Red Blood Cell.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.160
Their structures, shapes, sizes are totally

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.460
different from each other, and so are their

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.220
functions!

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.880
This is how various types of cells come together

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.580
in different numbers to form our body.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.990
We have this knowledge today!

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:11.390
But ever wondered how all this was actually discovered?

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.547
Let us go back in time, and have a look at

00:02:13.547 --> 00:02:15.190
the history of cellular studies.

